  "findings": [
    "In both diagnosed failures, early physical writes average about5 times the native text update RMS and have sampled-position cosine about0.998. This is a relative update-scale comparison, not a universal acceptable-ratio rule.",
    "C routing-token cosine is0.346/0.377 and execution-token cosine about0.93. Mid-layer read values have position cosine0.774/0.827, while final physical writes reach0.976/0.985. The state-product plus output mapping concentrates update directions; these data do not isolate the linear output projection alone.",
    "The semantic prior preserves total C/reference PRIOR mass but does not preserve POSTERIOR C/reference attention mass after adding physical logits and applying softmax. In the balloon case at layer14, mean C mass increases from0.08315 to0.16595, approximately2 times. This is a measured simultaneous routing-and-strength change.",
    "Null native text has one EOS and bypasses the semantic prior; the prior-induced strength change occurs in the positive arm. Guided full-minus-null predictions therefore change, with early full/native conditional-difference cosine0.425 to0.733 in these cases. This difference includes native text and Qwen conditions and is not a pure semantic vector.",
    "All inspected physical writes and normal velocities are finite; latent/clean estimate RMS is not an unbounded explosion. The observed stripe failures should not be attributed to nonfinite arithmetic or insufficient numerical precision without separate evidence.",
    "Substituting frozen native Q causes a large first-step velocity intervention (2.245 and0.900 times the no-C velocity RMS); independent physical Q cannot be dismissed as unused. Whether it helps generation requires the ongoing paired16 result.",
    "Actual videos establish that disabling semantic routing removes stripes in both cases, while restoring the older Q refinement alone does not. Reference allocation and value execution need to be reviewed together; numeric improvements on striped videos do not qualify as success."
  ],
  "inference_repair_hypothesis": {
    "proposal": "Separate the already-learned C-versus-zero-reference allocation from within-C semantic redistribution. Preserve the original physical posterior C mass computed from physical logits and the original group/reference prior; apply semantic support only within C. No new learned gate, scalar amplitude cap or weight updates.",
    "basis": "The original design intended semantic addressing while preserving total prior mass, but measured posterior physical mass changes strongly. Same-checkpoint semantic-off removes the observed artifacts.",
    "status": "Mechanistically motivated proposal only; not yet implemented or generation-validated; it is not the final R15F design.",
    "limits": "Fixing the mass coupling alone may fail to restore requested processes or reach SA/PC/Joint targets. Review all pending controls and actual videos before choosing the next trained architecture."
  }
